    As successive heatwaves hit Europe, air-conditioning (AC) has emerged as a new front in the international â€œ culture war â€ over climate action. France, Germany and the UK have experienced record-breaking heat and thousands of heat-related deaths this summer, with June temperatures in many regions passing 40C. This has drawn attention to the relatively low rates of AC use in these countries â€“ and in Europe as a whole â€“ especially when compared to its widespread adoption in the US. Legacy newspapers , bloggers and even Elon Musk have all weighed in on â€œ European hostility â€ to AC, criticising Europeâ€™s â€œ cultural conservatism â€ and â€œ overbearing governments â€. Right-wing politicians, includin...

